ock_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the tracker-root recovery in `reduce_ticket` (currently `os.path.dirname(ticket_dir)`) as a layout-helper call site, so a sharded ticket resolves link/alias targets against the tracker root, not its shard container.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1778,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["reduce_ticket: `tracker_dir: str | None = os.path.dirname(ticket_dir) or None` with the inline comment 'ticket_dir is <tracker>/<ticket_id>, so the parent is the tracker root' — an assumption sharding breaks","Step 4 routes forward 'write/read path composition through the helper' but does not mention recovering the tracker root FROM a (now two-deep) ticket path"],"finding":"The plan does not name the reverse tracker-root derivation in `reducer._api.reduce_ticket` as a site that must change: it computes `tracker_dir = os.path.dirname(ticket_dir)` to drive alias/link resolution during replay, which for a sharded ticket at `<tracker>/<shard>/<id>` returns the shard container rather than the tracker root.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f376714e87dbb2e62","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation Plan step 4 (path composition) / src/rebar/reducer/_api.py:188","norm_id":"n408164beea0d14d1","priority":0.7778,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reducing a migrated/sharded ticket whose events contain alias-form link targets: process_link resolves against the shard container instead of the tracker root, silently degrading or mis-resolving link targets"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add the reverse derivation (ticket-path → tracker-root) to the `ticket_layout` helper's responsibilities in step 1/step 4 and route `reduce_ticket`'s `tracker_dir` through it.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"