g these are shard containers, so `_load_local_tickets` loads zero tickets, re-introducing the ad39 orphaning bug its own docstring (lines 240-244) documents.","Step 3 keeps resolver outputs separator-free, so these `os.path.join`/`/`-style compositions are the call sites requiring layout-helper routing."],"finding":"The step-4 reconciler inventory `_engine/rebar_reconciler/{__main__,transition_replay,local_label_intent,impossible_links}.py` omits two sibling files that compose/iterate flat `tickets/<id>` paths and would break under the sharded layout: `inbound_translate.py` and `reconcile_check.py`. Because `resolve_ticket_dir_name` (step 3) stays separator-free, these direct joins/iterations are exactly the sites the layout helper must reach; their absence indicates the file list was not derived exhaustively from the reference graph.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6a3373e4eafa36cc","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation Plan step 4: \"graph ... commands ... _engine/rebar_reconciler/{__main__,transition_replay,local_label_intent,impossible_links}.py\"","norm_id":"n365361cbe433e814","priority":0.7778,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["inbound_translate.py:185 not patched — inbound Jira status projection reads a flat `tracker_dir/ticket_id` that no longer exists on a sharded store, always returning 'open' and mis-projecting status to Jira.","reconcile_check.py:249 not patched — `_load_local_tickets` iterating shard containers finds no `.cache.json`, loads zero local tickets, and reports every binding as orphaned (the exact ad39 regression documented in the same function)."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Route inbound_translate.py's ticket_dir through the layout helper's existing-dir resolution and replace reconcile_check.py's direct `tracker_dir.iterdir()` with the helper's deterministic ticket iteration; add both to the step-4 inventory.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_con